# Config Encryption Anti-Patterns

## Storing secrets in plain text properties

```properties
# WRONG — anyone with file access sees the password
db.password=mysecret123
```

**Encrypt at rest: AES-256-GCM with key derived from user password + salt.**

## Hardcoding encryption key

```java
// WRONG — key in source code
SecretKey key = new SecretKeySpec("mykey12345678901".getBytes(), "AES");
```

**Derive key from user password via PBKDF2. Never hardcode.**

## Using ECB mode — patterns leak

```java
// WRONG — ECB reveals patterns in encrypted data
Cipher.getInstance("AES/ECB/PKCS5Padding");
```

**Use GCM: `Cipher.getInstance("AES/GCM/NoPadding")`. Authenticated encryption.**